# SCM syntax highlighting & preventing 3-way merges
# pixi.lock is machine-generated and ~15k lines. `merge=binary` stops git from
# attempting a three-way merge on it: a conflict there is never worth resolving
# by hand — take one side and re-run `pixi lock` against the merged manifest.
# The linguist hints keep it out of the repo's language statistics and collapse
# it in GitHub diffs.
pixi.lock merge=binary linguist-language=YAML linguist-generated=true

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even in a Windows checkout: CI runs them
# with bash on ubuntu-latest, where CRLF breaks `set -o pipefail` and shellcheck
# flags the endings (SC1017). The `shell-lint` and `beautysh` pre-commit hooks
# read the same files. Nothing here ships a script yet — the rule is in place so
# the first one is correct on arrival.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Notebooks are LF-normalised JSON, which is what pre-commit's
# pretty-format-json hook and the CI `notebooks` task produce. Without this pin
# a Windows checkout rewrites every line, so every notebook under
# `docs/examples/` shows up as a full-file diff.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
